Q: Flask: send_from_directory and also refresh the page A: <p>It is possible with a bit of JS and a cookie</p>
<p>In flask app we need to add a disposable cookie to our response.
I assume, that <code>get_file()</code> is called from clicking some button on index page:</p>
<pre class="lang-py prettyprint-override"><code>@app.route(&quot;/get_file&quot;, methods=['GET'])
def get_file():
        # all your code
        # ...

        # create Response object, so we can add a cookie
        response = flask.make_response(flask.send_from_directory(location[0], location[1], as_attachment=True))
        response.set_cookie('reload_page_now', '', max_age=60)  # 1 min
    return response


@app.route(&quot;/&quot;, methods=['GET'])
def index():
        # create Response object, so we can remove cookie
        #   to prevent constant reload loop
        #   &lt;https://tedboy.github.io/flask/generated/generated/flask.Response.delete_cookie.html&gt;
        response = flask.make_response(flask.render_template('index.html')
        response.delete_cookie('reload_page_now')
    return response
</code></pre>
<p>In Jinja2/HTML template we need add JS to the bottom:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;script&gt;
// this script will check every 100ms for cookie with name &quot;reload_page_now&quot;
// on success, it will stop looping and will reload page in 500ms

let intervalId;

function CheckForReloadCookie() {
    if (!!document.cookie.match('reload_page_now')) {
        setTimeout(() =&gt; window.location.reload(), 500);
        clearInterval(intervalId);
    }
};

intervalId = window.setInterval(CheckForReloadCookie, 100); // run every 100 ms
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Using umd globals with modules in a Typescript project A: <p>You can use the <a href="https://www.typescriptlang.org/tsconfig/#allowUmdGlobalAccess" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>allowUmdGlobalAccess</code></a> option in tsconfig.json, and add the library you're interested in to <a href="https://www.typescriptlang.org/tsconfig/#types" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>types</code></a>:</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>{
  &quot;compilerOptions&quot;: {
    // ...
    &quot;allowUmdGlobalAccess&quot;: true,  //Needed to avoid &quot;'L' refers to a UMD global...&quot; error
    &quot;types&quot;: [
      &quot;leaflet/index.d.ts&quot;  //Or whatever library you're interested in
    ]
  }
}
</code></pre>

Q: Spring Jdbc template setAutocommit(false) A: <p>See the example of how to set auto commit false </p>

<pre><code>&lt;bean id="database" class="org.springframework.jdbc.core.JdbcTemplate"&gt;
&lt;property name="dataSource"&gt;
    &lt;bean class="org.apache.commons.dbcp.BasicDataSource" destroy-method="close"&gt;
        ...
        &lt;property name="defaultAutoCommit" value="false" /&gt;
        ...
    &lt;/bean&gt;
&lt;/property&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>
ref:
<a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/10746377/spring-3-1-jdbctemplate-auto-commit-to-false">spring 3.1: jdbcTemplate auto commit to false.</a></p>

<p>You can also try the annotation based connection transaction management ?<br>
<a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/9649318/how-can-i-config-to-turn-off-autocommit-in-spring-jdbc">How can I config to turn off autocommit in Spring + JDBC?</a>  </p>

Q: Audio streaming in ios using AVPlayer A: <p>this line isn't necessary <code>self-&gt;player = [AVPlayer playerWithURL:url];</code></p>

<pre><code>- (void)viewDidLoad
{
[super viewDidLoad];

NSURL *url = [NSURL URLWithString:@"http://108.166.161.206:8826/stream.mp3"];

self-&gt;playerItem = [AVPlayerItem playerItemWithURL:url];
self-&gt;player = [AVPlayer playerWithPlayerItem:playerItem];
[player play];

}
</code></pre>

<p>also don't forget to add the NSAllowsArbitraryLoads key to info.plist</p>

